{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented on branch `f86e-loc-ceiling-pinning` at commit `7f9060bb705`, based on `origin/main` `f1fe7c6f587`.\n\n**The change (7 files, matching the declared file_impact):**\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md` — added the `loc-ceiling-pinning` antipattern to the recall list, with both ADR 0058 exemptions stated inline (the anti-fragmentation floor; the `read_limit()` single-sourced mirror) and the mixed `100 <= n <= 500` case called out explicitly. Added FP guard (xi) so the fixed forms are not flagged.\n- `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml` — 29 → 33 cases. One recall case (`R-loc-ceiling-pinned-literal`, seeded from the live `test_run_span.py` violation) paired with three no-fire cases: the floor, the `read_limit()` mirror, and a numeric payload budget that is not a file line count (guarding against the antipattern over-generalizing to every `<= N`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` — provenance appended to the `tests` `_comment`. Verified by diff that every non-comment value is byte-identical to `HEAD`: no threshold, posture, or `applies_to` change.\n- `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` — new author-facing section under the fail-open material, matching the precedent set by story 3fce.\n\n**The 5 violation sites, cleaned:**\n\n- `tests/unit/test_run_span.py` — `test_gate_dispatch_within_module_cap` deleted wholesale; the whole test existed only to pin `<= 800`.\n- `tests/unit/test_header_delivery.py` — `test_runner_stays_within_the_module_size_cap` deleted wholesale, same reason.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py` — the `<= 500` upper half and both `<= 800` assertions removed; the `100 <=` anti-fragmentation floor **retained**, with a comment naming ADR 0058 as the owner of the upper bound. The now-unused `line_counts` dict collapsed to a direct count of the one file the floor applies to.\n\n**The 2 non-violations, untouched** — `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch.py:137` (`len(base) + len(out) <= 500`, a payload budget) and `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py:93` (`elapsed_ms <= 500`, a wall-clock assertion inside a lint fixture). A post-change tree sweep confirms these two are the only remaining `<= 500`/`<= 800` matches under `tests/` and `scripts/`.\n\n**Verification so far:** `make lint` green (including all three ratchets). `pytest` on the 3 touched modules: 29 passed. `pytest -k \"eval_spec or eval_discipline or criteria_routing or overlay or guide\"`: 329 passed, 2 skipped. `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD`: OK. The eval spec parses and reports 33 dataset cases.\n\n`make verify` and a local `rebar review-code` preview are running now. Not yet pushed to Gerrit.\n\n**Note on the AC design**, repeated here because it is the easiest thing for a later reader to get wrong: there is deliberately **no test asserting the antipattern's text is present in the shipped overlay**. The overlay's own Rule-5 litmus holds that an LLM is not a non-human consumer, so a prose grep guarding the author's wording is the change-detector the rubric exists to flag. The precedent commit `4c57247ff88` touched no `tests/` file at all for the same reason. Verification is by the paired recall/no-fire eval cases instead."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793728038006469536,"uuid":"ddcdf2e8-a700-415c-97bc-83086fac2868"}